        "body": "Appian Corp is a public company headquartered in McLean, Virginia, and trades under the ticker APPN. According to its website, it provides AI automation for business processes at large organizations, letting customers orchestrate AI agents, systems, and people from a unified platform. The company says it has been automating processes for more than 25 years.\n\nThe site describes a platform built around process automation, artificial intelligence, and legacy application modernization. Appian says customers can build AI-powered applications without code and embed AI agents that extract data, act autonomously, and generate code from natural language prompts. It also lists uses in finance and accounting, sourcing and procurement, audit and compliance, case resolution, purchase-to-pay, onboarding, order management, and contract review. The company states it was named a Leader in the 2025 Gartner Magic Quadrant for Business Orchestration and Automation Technologies (BOAT) and points to an AI Value Study produced with Harvard Business Review Analytic Services. It claims onboarding work can be cut by up to 50 percent.\n\nThe company's litigation exposure is in Virginia, with 129 matters. No individual lawsuits are named in the available material, and no specific products or MCP servers are listed. Its SEC central index key is 0001441683.",
